.TH SMSHEET 1
.SH NAME
smsheet \- lay views on sheets as PostScript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smsheet
.I part.draw
[
.I views
]
.br
.B smsheet \-r
.I part.draw
.br
.B smsheet \-v
.I part.draw
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Smsheet
reads a drawing file,
.IR draw (5),
and views from
.IR smdim (1)
in the file
.I views
or on the standard input
(one per view record, in order; then, if further scales are offered,
all again at each, largest first),
and writes a PostScript page for each sheet: the template, the views,
and on sheet 1 the notes.
.PP
A sheet is drawn at the largest scale at which its views fit the
template and, below scale 1, no ordinate text stands more than .75 in
from its place.
The views of a sheet are arranged in third-angle projection around the
front view, .4 in apart and .25 in clear of the notes and the kept
regions; a view with
.B at
is placed at the given point.
.PP
The lettering is osifont, to be found by Ghostscript with
.BI \-sFONTPATH= dir ,
as in the fonts of the library,
.IR plicad-lib (7).
.TP
.B \-r
Print the width and height of the room for views in the template,
in inches; no views are read.
.TP
.B \-v
Print what
.IR smdraw (1)
needs of the drawing file: a line
.BI units " unit unit"
(the second \- if none),
.BI scale " s"
or
.BR "scale \-" ,
.BI unmarked " material"
or
.BR "unmarked \-" ,
and for each view a line
.BI view " line name"
.BR \-h | \-
.IR scale | \-
(its line in the file, whether it shows hidden lines, and its own
scale), each of its records for
.IR smdim (1)
after it, its lengths in inches, after a line
.BI #line " n file" .
.SH SEE ALSO
draw(5), smdim(1), smdraw(1), gs(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
FILE:LINE: and the fault, for a bad record of the drawing file.
If no scale fits, the size of the views at the smallest scale is given
with the room of the template.
